# AM Berkeley SoftFloat library

This AM library fetches Berkeley SoftFloat commit
`a0c6494cdc11865811dec815d5c0049fba9d82a8` on first use and builds it for the
selected RISC-V `-march`/`-mabi`. The checkout under `repo/` and all build
outputs are ignored.

Consumers add `softfloat` to AM's `LIBS`. The result is a normal archive;
SoftFloat keeps operations in separate object files and the AM ABI adapter is
compiled with `-ffunction-sections`. Together with AM's `--gc-sections` link,
only referenced floating-point operations are retained in the final image.
